{
  "widgets": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 0,
      "width": 24,
      "height": 3,
      "properties": {
        "markdown": "# WNXT Prod20 \u2014 Infrastructure Dashboard (CPU / Memory / Network)\nCovers all Prod20 role servers plus the auto-scaling **WNXT-PROD20-USER-ASG** user fleet.\n\n**Note:** Memory widgets require the CloudWatch Agent to be installed and reporting to the `CWAgent` namespace (`mem_used_percent`) on each instance \u2014 if the agent isn't installed yet, those panels will show \"No data\". CPU, Network and Disk widgets use default EC2 metrics and need no agent."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3,
      "width": 24,
      "height": 1,
      "properties": {
        "markdown": "## Section 1 \u2014 Auto Scaling User Fleet (`WNXT-PROD20-USER-ASG`)\nInstances in this ASG are created/terminated automatically, so these widgets use **search expressions** keyed on the `AutoScalingGroupName` dimension rather than fixed Instance IDs \u2014 they will always reflect whichever instances are currently in the group, including newly launched ones."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "metric",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 4,
      "width": 6,
      "height": 6,
      "properties": {
        "title": "ASG CPU Utilization \u2014 Average across fleet (%)",
        "view": "timeSeries",
        "stacked": false,
        "region": "us-east-1",
        "period": 60,
        "yAxis": {
          "left": {
            "min": 0
          }
        },
        "metrics": [
          [
            {
              "expression": "SEARCH('{AWS/EC2,AutoScalingGroupName} MetricName=\"CPUUtilization\" AutoScalingGroupName=\"WNXT-PROD20-USER-ASG\"', 'Average', 60)",
              "label": "ASG CPU Utilization \u2014 Average across fleet (%)"
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "metric",
      "x": 6,
      "y": 4,
      "width": 6,
      "height": 6,
      "properties": {
        "title": "ASG CPU Utilization \u2014 Per Instance (%) \u2014 requires CWAgent",
        "view": "timeSeries",
        "stacked": false,
        "region": "us-east-1",
        "period": 60,
        "yAxis": {
          "left": {
            "min": 0
          }
        },
        "metrics": [
          [
            {
              "expression": "SEARCH('{CWAgent,InstanceId,AutoScalingGroupName} MetricName=\"cpu_usage_active\" AutoScalingGroupName=\"WNXT-PROD20-USER-ASG\"', 'Average', 60)",
